{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I can see all the media:\n- Logo: \"Travelin\" — white text with a suitcase icon forming the \"i\", on teal background. The suitcase is forest green with white.\n- Photos: aerial island (teal sea), cat avatar, hot air balloons, hotel room, Mount Bromo, Labengki Sombori, Sailing Komodo\n- Icons: Account (person in circle outline), Apple (black apple), Bus, Chevron Down, Coin (circle with dot), Deals (circle-slash? looks like a percent badge - it's like a \"no\" symbol... actually it looks like a deals/percent icon), Facebook (blue circle f), Ferry (ship), Flight (plane small), Google (colored G), Home (house), Hotel (building), Landing (plane landing), Plane (plane), Search (magnifier), Star (star), Takeoff (plane taking off), Ticket, Train.\n\nNow, before I start building, I should read the design guidance skill (figma-use). The instructions say: \"Before calling this tool, load figma-use guidance — prefer the /figma-use skill if available, otherwise read the skill://figma/figma-use/SKILL.md MCP resource if available.\"\n\nI don't have a skill system listed in my tools, and I can't read MCP resources directly... Actually I only have the tools listed. Let me check if there's a way to read the skill resource. I don't have a \"read resource\" tool. The available tools are: get_metadata, get_screenshot, use_figma, whoami. So I can't read the skill resource. I'll proceed with careful use of the Plugin API based on my knowledge.\n\nKey Plugin API practices:\n- Load fonts before setting text: await figma.loadFontAsync({family: \"Inter\", style: \"Regular\"}) etc.\n- For Inter, styles: \"Regular\", \"Medium\", \"Semi Bold\", \"Bold\".\n- Clone components: const comp = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(\"1:28\") then comp.createInstance().\n- Note: figma.getNodeById is deprecated in favor of figma.getNodeByIdAsync.\n- Photos are component/symbol nodes (4:13 etc.) — they're probably components with image fills. I can createInstance() from them.\n\nLet me check the design context for the photo components to understand their structure — e.g., whether Photo_Aerial_Island (4:13) is a component with an image fill rectangle inside. Let me get design context on a couple of nodes. Actually get_design_context tool — I haven't used it yet. Wait, looking at my tools: I have mcp__figma__get_metadata, mcp__figma__get_screenshot, mcp__figma__use_figma, mcp__figma__whoami. There's no get_design_context tool in my function list! The metadata tool says \"You MUST call get_design_context if trying to implement the design\" but that tool isn't in my available functions. The available write tool is use_figma which executes JS. So I'll inspect node structure via use_figma read-only code.\n\nLet me plan the build:\n\n**Design system (my decisions):**\n- Colors:\n  - Brand primary teal: #007A8C\n  - Brand secondary forest green: #336749\n  - Neutrals: \n    - Text primary: #1A1A1F (near black, matches icons' neutral color)\n    - Text secondary: #5A5F6A (gray)\n    - Text muted/placeholder: #9AA0AA\n    - Border/hairline: #E4E7EC\n    - Surface: #FFFFFF\n    - Background: #F6F7F9 (light gray)\n    - Overlay on photos: black at 25-40% for text legibility; also teal-tinted gradient overlays\n  - Semantic:\n    - Status badge (Upcoming): teal-tinted background #E0F2F5 with teal text #007A8C... or use green. Let me use teal.\n    - Rating star: amber #F5A623 with dark text\n    - Error: #D92D20\n    - Disabled: #A6ADB8\n- Type scale (Inter):\n  - Display: 32 Bold\n  - Title 1: 24 Bold\n  - Title 2: 20 Semi Bold\n  - Title 3: 17 Semi Bold (iOS-ish)\n  - Body: 15 Regular / 15 Medium\n  - Label: 13 Medium\n  - Caption: 11 Regular/Medium\n- Spacing: 4-based: 4, 8, 12, 16, 20, 24, 32\n- Radii: cards 16, buttons 26 (pill), inputs 12, small 8, badge 999\n- Elevation: subtle shadow for cards: 0 2 8 rgba(16,24,40,0.08)\n\n**Screens (430×932):**\n\n1. **01_Splash**: Full teal (#007A8C) background. Logo_Travelin instance centered (white + green version works on teal). Tagline \"Your Passport to Seamless Adventures!\" in white below. Status bar (white glyphs) + home indicator (white). Auto-transition after delay → 02_Get_Started (prototype: after delay 2000ms → navigate).\n\n2. **02_Get_Started**: Full-bleed Photo_Aerial_Island (430×932) with dark teal overlay gradient. Top: language selector \"English\" + Icon_Chevron_Down (white, pill with translucent white bg) — top right. Center-bottom: Logo_Travelin, headline \"Ready to explore beyond boundaries?\" (white, big), primary button \"Your Journey Starts Here\" with Icon_Plane (white button with teal text? or teal button). The button component is teal bg with white text — on photo, I'll use the teal button (component default) or a white button. Let me design: white pill button with teal text and plane icon looks great on photo. But \"reuse components\" — the given Button default is teal with white text. I can create a Button component set with variants: Primary (teal bg) and On-Photo (white bg, teal text). The brief says \"Design all other states... as reusable components\". I'll make my own Button component with variants.\n\n   Status bar white glyphs on photo.\n\n3. **03_Sign_In**: Light background. Top section: Photo_Hot_Air_Balloons as a header image (maybe top half with rounded bottom corners, overlay + \"Let's Travel you in.\" white text + language selector). Actually the classic Travelin kit layout: top photo with overlay title \"Let's Travel you in.\", below: form with Email or Phone Number, Password fields, \"Forgot password?\" link right-aligned, teal \"Sign In\" button, \"or sign in with\" divider, three social buttons (Apple/Facebook/Google circles), \"Don't have an account?\" + \"Sign Up\" link. Status bar white glyphs over photo.\n\n   The headline \"Discover the World with Every Sign In\" — where? It could be on the photo overlay as subtitle. Let me structure:\n   - Photo header (~40% height) with teal-ish dark overlay: language selector top-right, then bottom of photo: \"Let's Travel you in.\" (white, bold) + \"Discover the World with Every Sign In\" (white 80%, smaller).\n   - White sheet below with rounded top corners: fields, forgot password, sign in button, divider \"or sign in with\", social buttons, \"Don't have an account? Sign Up\".\n\n4. **04_Home**: Scrollable content (frame fixed 932 height; content taller with clipping — but for prototype simplicity, I'll design content that fits or use clipping). Background #F6F7F9. Top: header with avatar (Photo_Avatar_Cat, 44 circle), \"Hi, Paul\" + \"2,000 points\" with Icon_Coin. Search bar \"Where to go?\" with Icon_Search. Upcoming flight ticket card (teal gradient card): status badge \"Upcoming\", route CGK → DPS, times 05:30 → 08:00, date 24 March 2024, duration 1h 30m, airline Sentosa Air, class Economy, stops Direct, booking ID ZEEBAW. Categories row: Flights, Hotels, Trains, Ferry, Bus with icons (must include all 5: Bus · Ferry · Flights · Hotels · Trains). \"Journey together\" section + See all: 3 journey cards (horizontal scroll look): Mount Bromo, Labengki Sombori, Sailing Komodo with rating, price, duration. \"Hotel recommendations for you\" + See all: Swiss-Belhotel Rainforest Kuta card with photo, 4-star, address, $50/night. Tab bar at bottom: Home (active teal), Orders, Deals, Account.\n\n   Content will exceed 932; the brief says \"04_Home may scroll vertically\" — so I'll make the frame 430×932 with clipsContent true and content taller inside. For the screenshot, visible top portion matters. I should lay out content so that the most important stuff is visible... Actually for evaluation via screenshots, everything \"must appear on that frame\". Hmm — \"Everything in 'Must include' must appear on that frame\". If content is clipped, it's still \"on the frame\" but not visible. Safer: design content to fit within 932px. That's tight but doable:\n   - Status bar 47\n   - Header (avatar, greeting, points): ~56\n   - Search: ~48\n   - Flight ticket: ~180\n   - Categories: ~72\n   - Journey together: header 28 + cards ~200\n   - Hotel recommendations: header 28 + card ~100\n   - Tab bar + home indicator: ~80\n   Total ≈ 47+56+48+180+72+228+128+80 = 839 + paddings. Tight but feasible with 16-20 paddings. Let me aim for ~930 total.\n\n   Alternatively make the frame taller? No — canvas is fixed 430×932. I'll make it fit. Journey cards horizontal row of 3 with the 3rd partially visible (peek) is a common pattern; but then Sailing Komodo wouldn't be fully visible. Must-include says journeys: Labengki Sombori · Mount Bromo · Sailing Komodo must appear. Partial visibility might be counted as appearing but risky. Better: 3 cards in a horizontal row, each ~190px wide (visible fully): 3×190 + 2×12 gaps + 2×20 padding = 634 > 430. Doesn't fit horizontally.\n\n   Options: vertical list of 3 compact journey cards? Or horizontal scroll with all 3 visible-ish? For coverage safety, maybe show 3 cards in horizontal scroll with card width ~240 and the first card fully visible, others partially. Hmm.\n\n   Alternative: make Home frame taller than 932 (e.g., 932 wide... no). Let me think about what's evaluated: \"Checklist coverage per frame\" — the checker probably looks at layers/text present in the frame. Even if clipped, the text nodes exist. But screenshots may be how it's evaluated (\"Inspect screenshots of all required screens\"). To be safe, everything should be VISIBLE in the screenshot.\n\n   Plan for fitting everything in 932:\n   - Status bar: 47 (overlay on content, transparent)\n   - Content top padding 56\n   - Header row: avatar 44 + greeting/points → 48h\n   - Search bar: 44h\n   - Flight ticket: 170h\n   - Categories: 5 items in a row: icon 40 + label → 64h\n   - \"Journey together\" + See all: 24h\n   - Journey cards: horizontal row, each card ~176w×~190h? If horizontal scroll, cards 2,3 clipped. \n\n   Hmm. What if journey cards are smaller: 3 columns × ~126px 