 bottom y=932-34-16-52. Icon_Plane inside button left of text (teal colored). My Button component needs optional icon slot — simpler: place icon instance over button instance? Cleaner: create special \"CTA button\" as part of frame with auto-layout (white pill, gap 8, plane icon + text). But component reuse... The Button component set is used for \"Sign In\". The CTA has icon — I'll add a third Style variant \"OnPhoto Icon\"? Hmm. Simplest: Button variants text-only; the Get Started CTA = Button OnPhoto instance + Icon_Plane instance placed on top (absolute). With auto-layout button, absolute icon overlay is fragile. \n    Alternative: build CTA row as auto-layout frame directly in the Get Started frame (not a component). Acceptable — but \"component reuse\" evaluated. I'll make Button component set have property \"Icon=None/Plane\"? Component set variants: Style(Primary/OnPhoto) × State(Default/Pressed/Disabled) × Icon(No/Yes) = 12 variants — too many. \n    Pragmatic: Button set with Style×State (6). The CTA button in 02: instance of Button OnPhoto with text \"Your Journey Starts Here\", and I add Icon_Plane (teal) absolutely positioned left of the text? With auto-layout centered text, icon placement: I'll make the Button component an auto-layout with horizontal center; I can add the icon as a child of the INSTANCE? Instances can't add children. \n    OK simplest robust: create a separate component \"Button CTA\" (white pill with plane icon + teal text, 358×52) used once. And note Button set for other buttons. Fine — it's still a reusable component.\n\n    Layout 02: photo full; scrim; language selector top right; bottom stack (auto-layout vertical, x=36, width 358, bottom area): Logo 180w centered? Left aligned? Center: logo centered (y ~640), headline centered (26 Bold, 2 lines, y ~715), spacing 28, CTA button y=846-52 → y=814? home indicator at 898-932. Button bottom margin: 932-34(home ind)-16 = 882 → button y=830, height 52. Headline above: y=830-24-72=734 (2