820. \n    Let me verify vertical budget: 64 header top +48 header =112; +16 → search 128..172; +16 → ticket 188..364 (h176); +20 → categories 384..448 (64); +22 → section header 470..494; +8 → cards 502..672 (170); +20 → header 692..716; +8 → hotel 724..820; tab bar 834. \n\n**Prototype links:**\n- 01_Splash frame: AFTER_TIMEOUT 2000 → 02_Get_Started (Navigate). \n- 02: CTA button instance → 03_Sign_In.\n- 03: Sign In button instance → 04_Home.\n- 04: none.\n\nAlso make frames interactive starting point: set 01_Splash as flow start? In plugin API, set frame.prototypeStartNode? Actually flowStartingPoints on node? For prototype, you can set `figma.currentPage.prototypes`? Hmm: plugin API: `node.prototypeStartNode = true`? There's `prototypeStartNode` property on FrameNode? I recall `frame.prototypeStartNode = true` is not a thing; flows are defined via `figma.root` ... Actually there's `PrototypeDevice` on page? Setting flow start: In the plugin API, `frameNode.prototypeStartNode`? Hmm, I believe it's `node.prototypeStartNode` — no wait. There's \"flowStartingPoints\" on PageNode? Let me think... Figma plugin API has `page.prototypes`? I remember: `figma.currentPage.prototypeStartNode`? Not sure. There IS `frame.prototypeStartNode`? Searching memory: The API reference lists \"prototypeStartNode: boolean\" on... hmm, actually I recall in rest API \"prototypeStartNode\" is a property of FrameNode in the document JSON. In plugin API, FrameNode has `flowStartingPoints`? No that's not it either.\n\nI'll attempt: `frame.prototypeStartNode = true` inside try/catch — if it throws, skip (prototype still works by clicking frames).\n\nReactions: \n```js\nnode.reactions = [{\n  trigger: {type: 'ON_TAP'},\n  action: {type: 'NODE', destinationId: 'XX', navigation: 'NAVIGATE', transition: null, preserveState: false}\n}];\n```\ntransition: null might be invalid — omit? Action type NODE: {type:'NODE', destinationId, navigation:'NAVIGATE', transition, fetchResponse...}. I'll include transition: {type:'MOVE_IN', direction:'LEFT', duration:0.3, easing:{type:'EASE_OUT'}}... The Easing type in newer API: {type:'EASE_OUT', easingFunction:{type:'BEZIER',...}}? To be safe use transition: null → instant. Hmm \"transition: null\" — I've seen examples with `transition: null` being accepted? Actually in the typings, `transition` is optional. Omit it entirely.\n\nFor AFTER_TIMEOUT: trigger {type:'AFTER_TIMEOUT', timeout: 2000}. If it throws, fallback ON_TAP with whole-frame? I'll try-catch.\n\n**Recolor helper** for icon instances:\n```js\nfunction recolor(node, hex) {\n  const paint = {type:'SOLID', color: hexToRgb(hex)};\n  for (const v of node.findAll(() => true)) {\n    if ('fills' in v && Array.isArray(v.fills) && v.fills.length) v.fills = v.fills.map(f => f.type==='SOLID' ? {...paint, opacity:f.opacity} : f);\n    if ('strokes' in v && Array.isArray(v.strokes) && v.strokes.length) v.strokes = v.strokes.map(s => s.type==='SOLID' ? {...paint, opacity:s.opacity} : s);\n  }\n}\n```\nNote: findAll on instance returns children (overridable). Setting fills on instance sublayers allowed.\n\nBut careful: icon components with invisible fills on root — skip root.\n\n**Text setting**: need fonts loaded: Inter Regular, Medium, Semi Bold, Bold. Also the library text uses fontName {Inter, Semi Bold}. When changing characters of instance text, must load that font.\n\n**Creating components**: figma.createComponent(); comp.resize...; append children; comp.name = \"Button\"; for sets: figma.combineAsVariants(nodes, parent) then set variant properties via componentProperties? combineAsVariants creates ComponentSet; then rename children to \"Style=Primary, State=Default\" etc.\n\nGiven the size of this build, I'll do it in ~6 use_figma calls. Let me be careful about errors; keep each call focused and log progress.\n\nAlso hexToRgb helper each call (code doesn't persist between calls — each call is separate sandbox? State persists in the file, not JS. I'll redefine helpers per call.)\n\nAlso — placement: components at x=-1200 (left of frames) on same page, organized grid; frames at x=100.. with 480 step. Or components BELOW at y=1150. Screenshot of page will show everything; fine.\n\nLet me also decide point sizes for time display etc. OK.\n\nData check (verbatim):\n- \"Your Passport to Seamless Adventures!\" ✓\n- \"Your Journey Starts Here\" ✓\n- \"Ready to explore beyond boundaries?\" ✓\n- \"English\" ✓\n- \"Let's Travel you in.\" — note the curly apostrophe ' in brief: \"Let's Travel you in.\" I'll use \"Let's Travel you in.\" with U+2019.\n- \"Discover the World with Every Sign In\" ✓\n- \"Email or Phone Number\" / \"Password\" ✓\n- \"Forgot password?\" / \"Sign In\" / \"or sign in with\" / \"Don't have an account?\" (curly apostrophe: \"Don't have an account?\") / \"Sign Up\" ✓\n- Home: \"Hi, Paul\", \"2,000 points\", categories Bus/Ferry/Flights/Hotels/Trains, \"Hotel recommendations for you\", \"See all\", \"Swiss-Belhotel Rainforest Kuta\", \"Journey together\", \"Labengki Sombori\", \"Mount Bromo\", \"Sailing Komodo\", \"Where to go?\", tabs Home/Orders/Deals/Account.\n- Flight: \"Upcoming\", \"24 March 2024\", \"CGK\", \"05:30\", \"DPS\", \"08:00\", \"1h 30m\", \"Sentosa Air\", \"Economy\", \"Direct\", \"Booking ID: ZEEBAW\" (label \"Booking ID\" + value \"ZEEBAW\").\n- Journeys: \"Mount Bromo\" \"Volcano in East Java\" \"4.9\" \"Start from $150/pax\" \"3D2N\"; \"Labengki Sombori\" \"Islands in Sulawesi\" \"4.8\" \"Start from $250/pax\" \"3D2N\"; \"Sailing Komodo\" \"Labuan Bajo\" \"4.8\" \"Start from $200/pax\" \"3D2N\".\n- Hotel: \"Swiss-Belhotel Rainforest Kuta\" \"4-star hotel\" \"Jl. Sunset Road No. 101, Kuta, Bali, Indonesia\" \"$50/night\".\n\nRatings: star icon + number.\n\n\"Upcoming flight\" heading on the ticket — the data block title is \"Upcoming flight\"; include label \"Upcoming flight\" on card. Good.\n\nLet me start building. Call 1: create components batch 1 (Button set, Button CTA, Text Field set, Language Selector set, Status Badge, Search Bar, Section Header, Social Button). \n\nActually, let me think about how to structure code robustly. Each use_figma call is sandboxed JS with figma global. I'll define helpers each time.\n\nAlso important: appending nodes to page 6:2: `const page = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('6:2'); page.appendChild(node);`\n\nFonts: load once per call as needed.\n\nLet me write Call 1: Button set (6 variants) + Button CTA + Text Field set (4 variants).\n\nButton variant structure: auto-layout frame, horizontal center-center, padding, w=358 h=52 fixed, radius 26, fill teal. Text child \"Sign In\" 16 SB white.\n\nCode sketch:\n\n```js\nawait figma.loadFontAsync({family:'Inter',style:'Regular'});\nawait figma.loadFontAsync({family:'Inter',style:'Medium'});\nawait figma.loadFontAsync({family:'Inter',style:'Semi Bold'});\nawait figma.loadFontAsync({family:'Inter',style:'Bold'});\nconst page = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('6:2');\nconst hex=(h)=>{const n=parseInt(h.slice(1),16);return{r:((n>>16)&255)/255,g:((n>>8)&255)/255,b:(n&255)/255}};\nconst solid=(h,o=1)=>({type:'SOLID',color:hex(h),opacity:o});\nconst CX=-1250, CY=100; // components area\n\nfunction makeButton(style, state, x, y){\n  const c = figma.createComponent();\n  c.name = 'Button';\n  c.resize(358,52);\n  c.layoutMode='HORIZONTAL';\n  c.primaryAxisAlignItems='CENTER';\n  c.counterAxisAlignItems='CENTER';\n  c.primaryAxisSizingMode='FIXED';\n  c.counterAxisSizingMode='FIXED';\n  c.cornerRadius=26;\n  let bg,fg;\n  if(style==='Primary'){ bg = state==='Default'?'#007A8C':state==='Pressed'?'#005F6D':'#D8DDE2'; fg = state==='Default'?'#FFFFFF':state==='Pressed'?'#FFFFFF':'#8A9097'; }\n  else { bg = state==='Default'?'#FFFFFF':state==='Pressed'?'#E9F1F2':'#FFFFFF66'; ... }\n```\n\nHmm OnPhoto disabled: bg white 40% (hex8 #FFFFFF66? Figma color with opacity — use solid('#FFFFFF',0.4)), text white 60%.\n\nSet fills via c.fills=[solid(bg)] or with opacity.\n\nText: const t=figma.createText(); t.fontName={family:'Inter',style:'Semi Bold'}; t.characters='Sign In'; t.fontSize=16; t.fills=[solid(fg)]; c.appendChild(t);\n\nPosition: c.x=x; c.y=y; page.appendChild(c);\n\nVariant naming: c.name = 'Style=Primary, State=Default';\n\nThen combineAsVariants([...], page) → set.name='Button'; position set at CX.\n\nText Field variants similar: 358×48, radius 12, white fill, strokes [solid('#E5E8EB')], strokeWeight 1, auto-layout HORIZONTAL, paddingLeft 16, counterAxisAlignItems CENTER. Text placeholder 15 Regular #8A9097.\n- Default: \"Email or Phone Number\"\n- Focused: stroke #007A8C weight 1.5, placeholder \"Email or Phone Number\"\n- Filled: stroke default, text \"paul@travelin.app\" color #1A1A1F, style Regular 15\n- Error: stroke #D92D20 1.5, text \"paul@travelin.app\" ink? + maybe caption. Keep border+value.\n\nLanguage selector: auto-layout H, padding H16 V8? size hug: w ~92 h 36, radius 18, gap 6, text \"English\" 13 M, chevron instance 16×16 recolored.\n- OnPhoto: fill #FFFFFF 22%, text white, chevron white\n- OnSurface: fill #FFFFFF, stroke #E5E8EB, text #1A1A1F, chevron #1A1A1F\n\nChevron: instance of 3:12 resized to 16×16? Native 20 — resizing instance 20→16 scales? Instance resize changes the instance size; vector child constraints may stretch. Icon vectors usually have SCALE constraint when built as icons; can't rely. Safer: keep 20×20 native. Component pill h=40 then. OK: chevron 20, padding H14, gap 6, height 40, radius 20.\n\nStatus Badge: auto-layout H, padding H12 V6, gap 6, fill #DFF0F2, radius 999, dot: ellipse 6×6 fill #007A8C, text \"Upcoming\" 11 SB #007A8C. Hmm — or use white version for ticket. Ticket badge: fill white 18%, text white, dot white. Make set \"Context=OnSurface/OnCard\"? Two variants: OnSurface (teal tint) and OnDark (white translucent). Good: property Context.\n\nSearch Bar: 358×44 auto-layout H, padding L16 R16, gap 10, center, fill white, radius 22, stroke #E5E8EB. Icon_Search instance (24 native) recolor #8A9097? Icon Search native 24×24 — in 44 bar fine. Text \"Where to go?\" 15 R #8A9097.\n\nSection Header: 358×24 auto-layout H spaceBetween, center: title 17 SB #1A1A1F (\"Journey together\"), \"See all\" 13 M #007A8C.\n\nSocial Button: 111×48 auto-layout center, white, radius 14, stroke #E5E8EB; icon instance centered (Apple 40 native → 40 in 48 ok; Facebook 40; Google 40). Native icon sizes 40×40. Hmm 40 in 48 is chunky; resize instance to 24? Scaling concerns again. Try resize to 24×24 — if the vector child has constraint SCALE it scales; if MIN/MAX it stays 40 and clips. Risk. Alternative: keep 40 native (button 48 high, 40 icon → tight but okay visually? padding 4). Looks big. Let me test resize behavior in inspection? Just try in code: create instance, resize, then check child size after; if child didn't scale, set child constraints... Actually simplest: set the instance's rescale! `instance.rescale(factor)` — rescale scales everything including children (like the scale tool K). rescale(0.6) on 40 → 24. rescale exists on nodes: node.rescale(scale). Yes! Use rescale for icons needing different sizes.\n\nGreat, rescale solves icon sizing: instance.rescale(24/40)=0.6.\n\nSimilarly Status Bar / Home Indicator stay native.\n\nLogo rescale: 254×76 → e.g. ×0.75 → 190×57.\n\nPhotos: instance.rescale to target then resize? For photos, FILL mode handles crop; just resize w/h (resize stretches frame; image FILL covers). Photo instance resize to any w/h fine.\n\nCategory Item: 68×64? auto-layout V center gap 6: tile: 48×48 auto-layout center, white fill, radius 14, stroke #E5E8EB; icon 20 (native) recolor #007A8C. Label 11 M #5B6167 hug.\nWidths: labels vary (Flights ~34px @11M). Card hug width. In frame, place 5 with equal spacing across 358: I'll wrap in an auto-layout row with spaceBetween? Auto-layout in frame: row 358 wide, 5 children, primaryAxisAlignItems 'SPACE_BETWEEN'. Row itself not a component; instances of Category Item inside.\n\nJourney Card: component 112×170? Auto-layout V: photo container 112×84 (radius 12, clip) containing photo instance 112×84; duration chip overlay on photo? Auto-layout children can't overlap; put chip as absolutely-positioned child (layoutPositioning='ABSOLUTE') in photo container — allowed in auto-layout frames. Chip: white 90% bg pill, \"3D2N\" 9 SB ink900, padding 6/3. \nBelow: name 12 SB #1A1A1F (h16, truncation? set textAutoResize 'NONE', textAlignHorizontal LEFT, width 112, height 16 → clips overflow silently... 12SB \"Labengki Sombori\" ~102px fits).\nLocation 10 R #8A9097, 2 lines fixed h26 (NONE resize, w112).\nRating row: star icon rescale to 12 (native 15 → rescale 0.8) recolor #F2B01E + \"4.9\" 11 SB #1A1A1F... data shows \"★ 4.9\". Text \"4.9\" 11 M.\nPrice: \"Start from $150/pax\" — 10 M, teal #007A8C. At 10M ≈ 92px fits 112.\nLayout paddings: photo, then padding 8: column gap 3, bottom pad 10. Height: 84+8+16+26+14+14+10 = 172.\nComponent name \"Journey Card\". Instances: override texts + swap photo + override rating/price/duration.\nPhoto swap: inside instance, find photo instance child, call swapComponent(photoComp). Since photo container has the photo instance as child with ABSOLUTE chip. swapComponent on nested instance: photoInst.swapComponent(newComp) — should work.\n\nText override: instance.findOne(n=>n.name==='Name').characters='Mount Bromo' — need font loaded. Also the text inside instance is nested in auto-layout — allowed.\n\nHotel Card: component 358×96 auto-layout H: photo container 120×96 (radius 14 left; set cornerRadius per-corner: topLeft 14 bottomLeft 14, others 0 — on the container with clipContent true) with Photo_Hotel_Room instance 120×96; content column padding 12 gap 4: name 13 SB (h18), \"4-star hotel\" 11 M #8A9097? Make it a mini-badge? Keep text. address 10 R #8A9097 w~200 h26 (2 lines), price \"$50/night\" 14 SB teal — bottom. Content column height 96, justify space-between? Use auto-layout V with paddingTop 12 bottom 10, gap 2, and price pinned bottom via spacer? 