{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I can see the transition branch requirements. The branch that accepts `destinationId` complains:\n\n\"Expected [0].action.transition to be one of the following, but none matched:\n  - Required value missing at [0].action.transition.easing\n  - Multiple issues: Invalid enum value. Expected 'MOVE_IN' | 'MOVE_OUT' | 'PUSH' | 'SLIDE_IN' | 'SLIDE_OUT', received 'DISSOLVE' at [0].action.transition.type; Required value missing direction; Required matchLayers; Required easing\"\n\nSo valid transition types: MOVE_IN, MOVE_OUT, PUSH, SLIDE_IN, SLIDE_OUT — each requiring direction, matchLayers?, easing. Also possibly SMART_ANIMATE with matchLayers+easing? The error listed enums for the directional ones. There's also a branch \"Required value missing at [0].action.transition.easing\" alone — that's probably SMART_ANIMATE or DISSOLVE variant requiring easing? Hmm: branch shows two alternatives:\n1. \"Required value missing at [0].action.transition.easing\" — a transition variant that only needs easing (maybe {type:'SMART_ANIMATE', matchLayers?, duration, easing} or DISSOLVE {duration, easing}?). Wait DISSOLVE was rejected as type... no — the second alternative lists the enum failure for DISSOLVE with the directional types. So variant 1 (only missing easing) — could be DISSOLVE or SMART_ANIMATE variant where only easing was missing (duration optional?). My DISSOLVE attempt had duration:0.2 but no easing, and it wasn't accepted because... if DISSOLVE variant only needed easing, adding easing would fix. But variant 2's enum expects MOVE_IN|MOVE_OUT|PUSH|SLIDE_IN|SLIDE_OUT for the directional variant which needs direction+matchLayers+easing.\n\nHmm wait — maybe the transition schema here doesn't have DISSOLVE at all. Variant 1: transition requiring only easing — that's probably SMART_ANIMATE: {type:'SMART_ANIMATE', duration?, easing, matchLayers?} — but matchLayers would be flagged... it says only easing missing, so matchLayers optional there. Or variant 1 could be {type:'DISSOLVE', duration, easing} — DISSOLVE with duration+easing where duration was provided (0.2 OK) and easing missing. That fits! Variant 1 = DISSOLVE (duration provided ✓, easing missing). Variant 2 = directional (type enum failed).\n\nSo: transition {type:'DISSOLVE', duration:0.2, easing:{type:'EASE_OUT', ...}}? Easing shape: Easing = {type:'EASE_IN_AND_OUT'|'EASE_IN'|'EASE_OUT'|'LINEAR'|'EASE_BACK'|'GENTLE'|'QUICK'|'BOUNCY'|'CUSTOM_CUBIC_BEZIER', ...}. For CUSTOM_CUBIC_BEZIER needs easingValue? Standard: {type:'EASE_OUT'} might work, or GENTLE/QUICK are also valid types.\n\nAlternatively, simplest: try transition:{type:'DISSOLVE',duration:0.2,easing:{type:'EASE_OUT'}}? Hmm — is 'EASE_OUT' a valid easing type in current API? Typings list Easing types: \"EASE_IN_AND_OUT\" | \"EASE_IN\" | \"EASE_OUT\" | \"LINEAR\" | \"EASE_BACK\" | \"GENTLE\" | \"QUICK\" | \"BOUNCY\" | \"CUSTOM_CUBIC_BEZIER\". Yes.\n\nBut also maybe simpler to avoid transition entirely — but the schema REQUIRES transition for NODE actions (it's in the error: the branch with destinationId requires transition). Actually wait — look at first attempt: action without transition → \"Expected [0].action.transition to be one of the following, but none matched: Required value missing at [0].action.transition\" — transition is required.\n\nOK so final shape:\n{trigger:{type:'ON_CLICK'}, action:{type:'NODE', destinationId, navigation:'NAVIGATE', transition:{type:'DISSOLVE', duration:0.2, easing:{type:'EASE_OUT'}}}}\n\nHmm, but does the AFTER_TIMEOUT trigger with 2000 remain valid? First attempt error mentioned trigger alternatives including AFTER_TIMEOUT+timeout missing — ambiguous. Let me just test one reaction with DISSOLVE+easing for the CTA; if OK, apply all.\n\nAlso prototypeStartNode doesn't exist on FRAME — the correct property per newer API might be on the reaction/flow. Setting flow starting point: In Plugin API, `frame.prototypeStartNode` doesn't exist... Actually the real API: PrototypeStoryboard? Flow starting points are stored in `figma.root.prototypeStartNode`? Hmm. Historically: `figma.root` has no such prop. There's `node.prototypeStartNode`? No. The modern way: reactions define flows via `flowStartingPoints` on page? Let me recall: PageNode has `prototypeStartNode`? I think PageNode.prototypeStartNode exists (deprecated?) — or `page.flowStartingPoints = [{nodeId, name}]`. Yes! PageNode.flowStartingPoints: readonly FlowStartingPoint[] — {nodeId: string, name: string}. That's the current API. So page.flowStartingPoints=[{nodeId: splash.id, name:'Travelin Flow'}].\n\nTry CTA test first.","signature":"04fd49225d334febb79ef6b8"}],"id":"87ce895f-1119-4e2e-ada9-0d669c179e44","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6b901ff1-9fdc-48e6-8bc5-70d16984c7d4","uuid":"7d94675c-ee8d-4362-8852-cd1e81d0af0b","timestamp":"2026-10-31T20:40:36.444Z","thinking_duration_ms":23545}
